  "source": "MONTAGE M Data List (montage_m_dl_H0.pdf, 'For firmware version 3.01 and later')",
  "source_pages": "27",
  "list": "Performance Category List",
  "notes": [
   "Main category numbers 0-15 follow the row order of the printed table; 16 = 'No Assign' (NoAsg), matching the MIDI 'Performance Main Category' / 'Part Main Category' parameter range 0-16 (default 16).",
   "Sub category numbers follow the printed column order within each main-category row (0 = first column). The MIDI Data Table gives 'Performance Sub Category' / 'Part Sub Category' a range of 0-7 with default 0 printed as '--', but the printed table has 9 columns for most rows (8 for Bass and Drum / Perc, which have one fewer specific sub category). The mapping of the trailing 'No Assign' column onto that 0-7 range is therefore UNVERIFIED from this document; the factory Performance List never uses 'No Assign' as a sub category.",
   "The last four named sub categories (Rock/Pop, R&B/Hip Hop, Electronic, Jazz/World) are common to every main category."
  ]
 },
